#!/usr/bin/env bash
# P-ATTR-01's STRUCTURAL half: the Protomaps credit is the plan's string, it is what the protomaps arm of
# MapStyle.attributionText returns, the demo arm returns the demo credit verbatim, nothing outside MapAdapter
# names a protomaps case, the LA basemap is mounted, the footer is handed the SAME resolved style the map is
# mounted with, and that footer is not hidden from accessibility. A source check on a box with no Apple
# toolchain (ruling R2), which decides eight things and refuses to pretend it decides more:
#   (a) THE ARM, not a count. Inside `public var attributionText: String`, the first line carrying code
#       after `case .protomapsLALight, .protomapsLADark:` is exactly `return MapStyle.protomapsAttribution`,
#       and the first after `case .maplibreDemoTiles:` is exactly `return MapStyle.demoAttribution`.
#       T-0195's mutant pass found every recorded grep blind to the arms trading places.
#   (b) THE TWO DECLARATIONS, as a WHITELIST OF WHOLE LINES. Every line naming `static let
#       protomapsAttribution` or `static let demoAttribution` anywhere under apps/ios is exactly one of the
#       two approved declarations, compared TRIMMED and WHOLE; and the plan's string occurs in code exactly
#       once over the tree. The pre-review mutant pass (2026-09-19, A2/A3) got both past a prefix and a
#       substring match: the demo credit set to a near-spelling of the Protomaps line, and the Protomaps
#       declaration keeping the literal and appending ` + " · Natural Earth"`. The demo credit may never
#       name OpenStreetMap contributors: the demo tiles carry no OpenStreetMap data. And a SECOND
#       population, because an identifier-keyed whitelist never saw rv1-pr119's M3: every `static let`
#       line under apps/ios whose value names OpenStreetMap IS that one approved declaration, so a
#       paraphrase declared under a new identifier is refused by name rather than counted by nobody.
#   (c) THE protomapsLA WHITELIST. Every occurrence of the identifier under apps/ios, counted with
#       multiplicity, against a tracked set typed here; and every occurrence OUTSIDE Sources/MapAdapter/ has
#       to sit on a `case .` pattern line. A feature target that NAMES a protomaps case builds a style
#       without asking `BasemapResolver` whether the archive is on the device, which is how the Protomaps
#       credit ends up over an empty map; one that MATCHES it reads the resolver's answer, which is what
#       `DriveCopy.mapCaption(for:style:)` does (ruling R0).
#   (d) THE MOUNT, AND ONE RESOLVED VALUE FOR BOTH HALVES. `BasemapResolver.losAngeles(` occurs exactly
#       once, in FeatureScenicHome/DriveBasemap.swift - without it the credit sits on no surface at all -
#       `DriveBasemap.resolve(` occurs exactly once, and every `AttributionFooter(` construction is read by
#       its ARGUMENT LIST, whose ONE approved form is `text: CreditLine.composed(basemap: <b>.attributionText,
#       routeData: <r>?.dataCredit)` - <b> the binding the map is mounted with (`styleURL: <b>.url`, once),
#       <r> the binding the one MapView( is handed as `route: <r>`. A5 of the mutant pass took the credit
#       from a SECOND `DriveBasemap.resolve(...)` while the map kept the first; rv1-t0236 B1 drew OpenStreetMap
#       geometry under the style's credit alone, which names MapLibre and Natural Earth without la.pmtiles.
#   (e) THE FOOTER IS NOT HIDDEN. Every occurrence of `accessibilityHidden` in DesignSystem/
#       AttributionFooter.swift and at the mount screen is `accessibilityHidden(false)`, and there is at
#       least one in the footer - acceptance bullet 2's own limb. `.accessibilityHidden(true)` is a licence
#       breach that renders identically in every screenshot (A7).
#   (f) EVERY MAP SURFACE, as a WHITELIST. What makes a surface a MAP surface is a `MapView(` construction
#       handed a `styleURL:`; what makes it a legal one is the footer beside it. Every occurrence of either
#       over apps/ios is at a site typed here - ScenicHomeScreen.swift(1) each - outside the ONE definition
#       site, MapAdapter/MapView.swift, which is itself pinned by `struct MapView` and `public
#       init(styleURL` occurring exactly once, there and nowhere else. rv1 of PR #119 (B2) mounted
#       `MapView(styleURL: style.url, ...)` in a SECOND file under FeatureScenicHome with no footer and
#       every limb above stayed green, because (d) counted `styleURL:` inside the mount screen alone: the
#       clause "every map surface carries the credit" was being asserted over one screen.
#   (g) THE DRAWN LINE'S CREDIT, as a WHITELIST OF WHOLE LINES (ops/lib/check-map-attribution-sites). Every
#       line under apps/ios naming `dataCredit`, `routeGeometryCredit` or the word `credit` is one of the typed
#       approved lines, compared TRIMMED and WHOLE with its file. (d) reads the credit's two ENDS; rv2-t0236 set
#       the VALUE between them to the demo credit in MapRoute.bundled (M4a) and to the resource name in
#       DriveRoute.resolve (M4b), and (a)-(f) stayed green.
#   (h) THE CREDIT ABOVE THE SHEET (ops/lib/check-map-attribution-sheet, T-0237): the pill and HomeSheet are the
#       approved five-line mount, pill first; one HomeSheet; the one presentation is the disclaimer sheet.
#       Then the render blocks - HomeSheet, the screen's body and its modifier chain - FROZEN whole (-frozen, rv2
#       B3); LAST the surface PINNED by content (ops/lib/check-safety-disclaimer-pinned, rv3-t0237): the file set
#       of FeatureScenicHome, each file's sha256 and AttributionFooter.swift's - a home-screen edit updates those
#       digests in the SAME commit. Rendering at both detents is T-0180's; a shadow outside the set is T-0243's.
#
# WHAT IT CANNOT SEE: whether the footer RENDERS, at which sheet detents, whether something is drawn over
# it, contrast, Dynamic Type, or whether the tiles on screen are the ones the credit names - an XCUITest in
# a simulator owns those (T-0180). Also unseen: `MapStyle.url` - which document each case actually hands the
# renderer, so a `url` arm swapped to the demo style is green here (A6); `/* */` comments; Swift outside
# apps/ios; a credit paraphrase that never names OpenStreetMap and a `static let` whose value sits on the
# NEXT line; a map mounted through some wrapper type that is not `MapView(`; whether a footer that IS built
# is visible - `.opacity(0)` beside it is green here (rv1-pr119's M2, T-0180's half); any spelling reaching a case
# unnamed, e.g. `MapStyle.allCases[0]` (A4; `MapStyle(rawValue: "protomapsLALight")` IS refused: (c) reads strings).
#
#   bash ops/lib/check-map-attribution                 # the tracked tree
#   bash ops/lib/check-map-attribution --app-tree DIR  # a copy of apps/ios (the mutation table hands one)
#   bash ops/lib/check-map-attribution --prove-red     # the mutations, each refused by name
set -uo pipefail
cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)"

LIB="ops/lib/check-map-attribution-lib"
SITES="ops/lib/check-map-attribution-sites"
SHEET="ops/lib/check-map-attribution-sheet"
for L in "$LIB" "$SITES" "$SHEET" ops/lib/check-safety-disclaimer-{frozen,pinned}; do
  if [[ ! -f "$L" ]]; then
    echo "P-ATTR-01: $L is missing; the check cannot read Swift source without its readers."
    exit 1
  fi
  . "$L"
done

DEFAULT_APP_TREE="apps/ios"
ADAPTER_REL="Packages/ScenicApp/Sources/MapAdapter"
FEATURE_REL="Packages/ScenicApp/Sources/FeatureScenicHome"
DESIGN_REL="Packages/ScenicApp/Sources/DesignSystem"
CREDIT="© OpenStreetMap contributors · Protomaps"
CREDIT_IDENT="static let protomapsAttribution"
CREDIT_DECL="public static let protomapsAttribution = \"$CREDIT\""
DEMO_IDENT="static let demoAttribution"
DEMO_DECL="public static let demoAttribution = \"© MapLibre · Natural Earth\""
PROTOMAPS_IDENT="protomapsLA"
# Typed literals in the scan's own path order, raised deliberately the day a target legitimately grows one
# more (the shape P-SAFE-03's whitelist uses, T-0153 ruling R4-B): a derived expectation moves whenever the
# thing it is derived from moves. MapStyle: two case declarations, two arms of `url`, two in the credit arm.
# MapAppearance: `protomapsStyle`'s two arms. DriveCopy: the caption's one pattern line, which carries two.
PROTOMAPS_SET="$FEATURE_REL/DriveCopy.swift(2) $ADAPTER_REL/MapAppearance.swift(2) $ADAPTER_REL/MapStyle.swift(6)"
CREDIT_SET="$ADAPTER_REL/MapStyle.swift(1)"
MOUNT_SET="$FEATURE_REL/DriveBasemap.swift(1)"
FOOTER_SET="$FEATURE_REL/ScenicHomeScreen.swift(1)"
SURFACE_SET="$FEATURE_REL/ScenicHomeScreen.swift(1)"
MAPVIEW_REL="$ADAPTER_REL/MapView.swift"
MIN_FILES=8

APP_TREE="$DEFAULT_APP_TREE"
PROVE_RED=0
while [[ $# -gt 0 ]]; do
  case "$1" in
    --app-tree) APP_TREE="${2:-}"; shift 2 ;;
    --prove-red) PROVE_RED=1; shift ;;
    *) echo "check-map-attribution: unknown argument: $1" >&2; exit 2 ;;
  esac
done
APP_TREE="${APP_TREE%/}"

fail() {
  echo "P-ATTR-01: $1"
  shift
  for extra in "$@"; do echo "  $extra"; done
  exit 1
}

# `grep -c`, never `-q`/`-l`, on either side of a pipe (P-OPS-03).
code_of() { sed -e 's/\r$//' -e 's|//.*||' "$1"; }
count_fixed_in() { code_of "$2" | grep -c -F -e "$1" || true; }

require_tracked_occurrences() {
  local needle="$1" kind="$2" expected="$3"
  shift 3
  local why=()
  while [[ $# -gt 0 && "$1" != "--" ]]; do why+=("$1"); shift; done
  [[ "${1:-}" == "--" ]] && shift
  local seen=() an="$#"
  mapfile -t seen < <(occurrences_with_multiplicity "$needle" "$@")
  [[ "${seen[*]}" == "$expected" ]] || fail \
    "the $kind $needle occurs outside its tracked set; found: ${seen[*]:-none}" \
    "Tracked set: $expected. Counted by OCCURRENCE - one line may carry two - over all $an .swift file(s)" \
    "under $APP_TREE with // stripped. This is a WHITELIST: any other count in any file is refused by name." \
    "${why[@]}"
}

run_check() {
  [[ -d "$APP_TREE" ]] || fail "no such directory: $APP_TREE" \
    "The pin's population is the app tree; a missing tree must never read as 'the credit is on the surface'."

  local map_style="$APP_TREE/$ADAPTER_REL/MapStyle.swift"
  local appearance="$APP_TREE/$ADAPTER_REL/MapAppearance.swift"
  local basemap="$APP_TREE/$FEATURE_REL/DriveBasemap.swift"
  local screen="$APP_TREE/$FEATURE_REL/ScenicHomeScreen.swift"
  local footer="$APP_TREE/$DESIGN_REL/AttributionFooter.swift"
  local f
  for f in "$map_style" "$appearance" "$basemap" "$screen" "$footer"; do
    [[ -f "$f" ]] || fail "missing file: $f" \
      "(a)-(e) name these five files. A tree without them is a refusal, never a pass."
  done

  local files=()
  mapfile -t files < <(find "$APP_TREE" -type f -name '*.swift' | LC_ALL=C sort)
  local an="${#files[@]}"
  [[ "$an" -ge "$MIN_FILES" ]] || fail "only $an .swift file(s) under $APP_TREE (expected >= $MIN_FILES)." \
    "A whitelist over a population that enumerated nothing is green for the wrong reason (P-SRC-02 shape)."

  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ (a) the ARM
  local pline pok dline dok
  read -r pline pok dline dok <<<"$(arm_verdict "$map_style")"
  [[ "$pline" -gt 0 ]] || fail \
    "no \`case .protomapsLALight, .protomapsLADark:\` inside attributionText in $map_style." \
    "The credit for the LA tiles is whatever that arm returns; with no arm there is nothing to anchor."
  [[ "$pok" -eq 1 ]] || fail \
    "the protomaps arm at line $pline of $map_style does not return MapStyle.protomapsAttribution." \
    "The first line carrying code after that \`case\` must read exactly \`return MapStyle.protomapsAttribution\`." \
    "Swapping the arms leaves every identifier and every count unchanged (T-0195's mutant pass) while the" \
    "LA basemap is credited to MapLibre and Natural Earth."
  [[ "$dline" -gt 0 ]] || fail "no \`case .maplibreDemoTiles:\` inside attributionText in $map_style." \
    "The fallback needs its own credit, or the demo tiles inherit somebody else's."
  [[ "$dok" -eq 1 ]] || fail \
    "the demo arm at line $dline of $map_style does not return MapStyle.demoAttribution." \
    "MapLibre's demo tiles carry no OpenStreetMap data and are not served by Protomaps: the plan's credit" \
    "under them credits two parties for country polygons neither drew - on every device without la.pmtiles."

  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ (b) the TWO DECLARATIONS
  require_one_declaration "$CREDIT_IDENT" "$CREDIT_DECL" "the credit literal is not declared verbatim" \
    "CLAUDE.md states the string: Attribution (\`$CREDIT\`) is visible on every map surface at every detent." \
    -- "${files[@]}"
  require_one_declaration "$DEMO_IDENT" "$DEMO_DECL" "the demo credit declaration is not verbatim" \
    "The demo tiles are MapLibre's, drawing Natural Earth country polygons: no OpenStreetMap data and no" \
    "Protomaps service. A demo credit naming OpenStreetMap contributors is a false credit on every device" \
    "without la.pmtiles and on the Skyline drive always - and it is invisible to a grep for the plan's" \
    "string, which is still declared once and still correct where it is." \
    -- "${files[@]}"
  require_tracked_occurrences "$CREDIT" "credit literal" "$CREDIT_SET" \
    "A credit string typed at a call site is right even over a blank map, so it is the one anchor that must" \
    "never be trusted alone: the string has to come from the RESOLVED style and from nowhere else." \
    -- "${files[@]}"
  require_osm_credit_whitelist "$CREDIT_DECL" -- "${files[@]}"

  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ (c) the protomapsLA WHITELIST
  require_tracked_occurrences "$PROTOMAPS_IDENT" "identifier" "$PROTOMAPS_SET" \
    "Naming a protomaps case outside MapAdapter builds a style without asking BasemapResolver whether the" \
    "archive is on this device, and the Protomaps credit then travels over an empty map." \
    -- "${files[@]}"
  local outside=()
  for f in "${files[@]}"; do
    case "$f" in "$APP_TREE/$ADAPTER_REL"/*) ;; *) outside+=("$f") ;; esac
  done
  local named=()
  mapfile -t named < <(awk -v needle="$PROTOMAPS_IDENT" -v root="$APP_TREE/" '
    {
      code = $0; sub(/\r$/, "", code); sub(/\/\/.*$/, "", code)
      if (index(code, needle) == 0) next
      if (code ~ /^[ \t]*case[ \t]+\./) next
      rel = FILENAME
      if (index(FILENAME, root) == 1) rel = substr(FILENAME, length(root) + 1)
      printf "%s:%d:%s\n", rel, FNR, code
    }
  ' "${outside[@]}")
  [[ "${#named[@]}" -eq 0 ]] || fail \
    "$PROTOMAPS_IDENT is NAMED outside $ADAPTER_REL/ on ${#named[@]} line(s), not matched as a pattern:" \
    "${named[@]}" \
    "Outside the adapter a protomaps case may only be MATCHED - reading the style the resolver returned -" \
    "never NAMED. The count whitelist alone cannot tell a pattern from a construction that keeps the count."

  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ (d) the MOUNT and the FOOTER
  require_tracked_occurrences "BasemapResolver.losAngeles(" "mount" "$MOUNT_SET" \
    "Without a call site the whole of MapAdapter is dead code: the credit is correct, the style resolves," \
    "and no surface in the app ever asks for either (T-0195's mutant pass, the reason T-0178 exists)." \
    -- "${files[@]}"
  require_tracked_occurrences "AttributionFooter(" "footer construction" "$FOOTER_SET" \
    "Every map surface carries the credit; a second footer somewhere else is a second string to keep true." \
    -- "${files[@]}"
  require_tracked_occurrences "DriveBasemap.resolve(" "resolve call" "$FOOTER_SET" \
    "ONE resolve per screen, held in state: a second call is a second answer, and the credit then names" \
    "tiles the renderer never got (mutant pass A5 - the footer resolved again, the map kept the first)." \
    -- "${files[@]}"

  require_composed_footer "$screen"
  local recv="$FOOTER_STYLE"
  local mounted styles
  mounted="$(count_fixed_in "styleURL: $recv.url" "$screen")"
  styles="$(count_fixed_in "styleURL:" "$screen")"
  [[ "$mounted" -eq 1 && "$styles" -eq 1 ]] || fail \
    "the map is not mounted with the same resolved value the credit came from: \`styleURL: $recv.url\`" \
    "occurs $mounted time(s) in $screen and \`styleURL:\` occurs $styles time(s), expected 1 and 1." \
    "The tiles and the credit are two halves of one fact: the footer reads $recv.attributionText, so the" \
    "renderer has to be handed $recv.url and nothing else."
  require_route_mount "$screen" "$FOOTER_ROUTE"

  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ (e) NOT HIDDEN from accessibility
  local all_h ok_h
  for f in "$footer" "$screen"; do
    read -r all_h ok_h <<<"$(hidden_counts "$f")"
    [[ "$all_h" -eq "$ok_h" ]] || fail \
      "$f hides something from accessibility: $all_h \`accessibilityHidden\` occurrence(s), $ok_h of them" \
      "\`accessibilityHidden(false)\`. Every occurrence must be \`(false)\` - a WHITELIST, so \`(true)\`," \
      "an interpolated argument and any other spelling are refused by name rather than blacklisted." \
      "A screen reader user is entitled to the same credit line as everybody else: ODbL's credit is not" \
      "satisfied by a footer that renders and is hidden from VoiceOver, and the screenshot is identical."
    if [[ "$f" == "$footer" ]]; then
      [[ "$ok_h" -ge 1 ]] || fail \
        "$footer never states \`accessibilityHidden(false)\`." \
        "Acceptance bullet 2 asks this check to assert that AttributionFooter is not accessibilityHidden." \
        "The explicit \`false\` is what makes its removal a visible deletion in a diff; left to the default," \
        "nothing here can tell 'not hidden' from 'nobody said'."
    fi
  done

  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ (f) EVERY MAP SURFACE
  require_map_mounts "$APP_TREE/$MAPVIEW_REL" "$MAPVIEW_REL" "$SURFACE_SET" -- "${files[@]}"

  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ (g) THE DRAWN LINE'S CREDIT, whole lines
  require_credit_sites -- "${files[@]}"

  # ------------------------------------------------------------------ (h) THE CREDIT ABOVE THE SHEET
  require_sheet_mount "$screen" -- "${files[@]}"
  require_frozen_blocks "$APP_TREE/$FEATURE_REL" "$APP_TREE"
  require_pinned_surface "$APP_TREE/$FEATURE_REL"

  print_verdict "$an" "$pline" "$dline" "$FOOTER_ARG" "$recv" "$FOOTER_ROUTE"
  print_credit_sites_verdict
  print_sheet_verdict
  echo "  Then HomeSheet, the screen's body, chips, sheetDetails, conditions and the app shell frozen whole; LAST"
  echo "  $PINNED_FILES FeatureScenicHome file(s) and AttributionFooter.swift pinned by sha256 (-pinned)."
}

MUTATIONS="ops/lib/check-map-attribution-mutations"
if [[ "$PROVE_RED" -eq 1 ]]; then
  [[ -f "$MUTATIONS" ]] || fail "$MUTATIONS is missing; --prove-red has no table to run."
  # A table run against an already-red tree prints refusals that prove nothing about the mutations. The probe
  # runs in a SUBSHELL because `fail` exits (the bug check-safety-disclaimer already paid for once).
  if ! ( run_check >/dev/null ); then
    echo "P-ATTR-01: --prove-red refuses to run against a tree that is already red."
    run_check
    exit 1
  fi
  exec bash "$MUTATIONS"
else
  run_check
fi
